DESCRIPTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Anteater Poker is an online multiplayer Texas Hold'em variant featuring
the UCI Anteater Wild Card mechanic. Players connect to a central server,
take a seat, and play against other humans or bots through a GTK3 GUI.

PACKAGE LAYOUT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  poker/
    Makefile     build and packaging targets
    README       this file
    COPYRIGHT    license / copyright
    INSTALL      detailed build & run instructions
    src/         source code and src/Makefile
    bin/         executables (created by `make`)
    doc/         PDF documentation

QUICK START
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
See INSTALL for full build instructions.

  1. Build from source (from inside poker/):
       make

  2. Start the server:
       ./bin/poker_server &

  3. Launch one or more clients:
       ./bin/poker_client

  4. On the login screen, enter your username, the server IP, and port
     (default: 127.0.0.1:9000), then click "Connect & Join Game".

  5. The server dashboard lets you add bots and deal new hands.

BUILD TARGETS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  make            Build poker_server and poker_client into bin/
  make test       Build and run the unit tests
  make test-gui   GUI smoke build
  make test-comm  Communication smoke build
  make clean      Remove build artifacts
  make tar        Create both source and binary release archives

ANTEATER WILD CARD RULE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
One player per hand is randomly dealt the Anteater Wild Card.
The Wild Card can substitute for any rank or suit to form the best
possible 5-card hand. If the Wild Card appears in the winning hand,
the winner receives a 200-point bonus on top of the pot.

